1
00:00:02,118 --> 00:00:08,035
(Q11（单选）) Right. Next on the agenda we have traffic and highways. Councillor Thornton.

2
00:00:08,035 --> 00:00:16,576
Thank you. Well, we now have the results of the survey carried out last month about traffic and road transport in the town.

3
00:00:16,576 --> 00:00:20,112
People were generally satisfied with the state of the roads.

4
00:00:20,112 --> 00:00:33,539
[Q11答案句] There were one or two complaints about potholes which will be addressed, but a significant number of people complained about the increasing number of heavy vehicles using our local roads to avoid traffic elsewhere.

5
00:00:33,539 --> 00:00:42,365
We'd expected more complaints by commuters about the reduction in the train service, but it doesn't seem to have affected people too much.

6
00:00:42,365 --> 00:00:52,179
(Q12) The cycle path that runs alongside the river is very well used by both cyclists and pedestrians since the surface was improved last year,

7
00:00:52,179 --> 00:00:58,337
[Q12答案句] but overtaking can be a problem so we're going to add a bit on the side to make it wider.

8
00:00:58,337 --> 00:01:08,072
At some stage, we'd like to extend the path so that it goes all the way through the town, but that won't be happening in the immediate future.

9
00:01:08,072 --> 00:01:16,072
(Q13) The plans to have a pedestrian crossing next to the Post Office have unfortunately had to be put on hold for the time being.

10
00:01:16,072 --> 00:01:19,667
We'd budgeted for this to be done this financial year,

11
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:26,751
but then there were rumours that the Post Office was going to move, which would have meant there wasn't really a need for a crossing.

12
00:01:26,751 --> 00:01:29,391
Now they've confirmed that they're staying where they are,

13
00:01:29,391 --> 00:01:38,965
[Q13答案句] but the Highways Department have told us that it would be dangerous to have a pedestrian crossing where we'd originally planned it as there's a bend in the road there.

14
00:01:38,965 --> 00:01:41,334
So that'll need some more thought.

15
00:01:41,334 --> 00:01:49,192
(Q14) On Station Road near the station and level crossing, drivers can face quite long waits if the level crossing's closed,&nbsp;

16
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:54,849
[Q14答案句] and we've now got signs up requesting them not to leave their engines running at that time.

17
00:01:54,849 --> 00:02:01,831
This means pedestrians waiting on the pavement to cross the railway line don't have to breathe in car fumes.

18
00:02:01,831 --> 00:02:13,652
We've had some problems with cyclists leaving their bikes chained to the railings outside the ticket office, but the station has agreed to provide bike racks there.

19
00:02:13,652 --> 00:02:20,502
(Q15（地图）) So next on the agenda is 'Proposals for improvements to the recreation ground'.

20
00:02:20,502 --> 00:02:23,002
Councillor Thornton again.

21
00:02:23,002 --> 00:02:33,135
Well, since we managed to extend the recreation ground, we've spent some time talking to local people about how it could be made a more attractive and useful space.

22
00:02:33,135 --> 00:02:41,550
If you have a look at the map up on the screen, you can see the river up in the north, and the Community Hall near the entrance from the road.

23
00:02:41,550 --> 00:02:56,931
At present, cars can park between the Community Hall and that line of trees to the east, but this is quite dangerous for pedestrians so we're suggesting a new car park on the opposite side of the Community Hall, right next to it.

24
00:02:56,931 --> 00:03:00,699
(Q16) We also have a new location for the cricket pitch.

25
00:03:00,699 --> 00:03:15,413
As we've now purchased additional space to the east of the recreation ground, beyond the trees, we plan to move it away from its current location, which is rather near the road, into this new area beyond the line of trees.

26
00:03:15,413 --> 00:03:20,489
This means there's less danger of stray balls hitting cars or pedestrians.

27
00:03:20,489 --> 00:03:29,008
(Q17) We've got plans for a children's playground which will be accessible by a footpath from the Community Hall and will be alongside the river.

28
00:03:29,008 --> 00:03:35,907
We'd originally thought of having it close to the road, but we think this will be a more attractive location.

29
00:03:35,907 --> 00:03:49,092
(Q18) The skateboard ramp is very popular with both younger and older children – we had considered moving this up towards the river, but in the end we decided to have it in the southeast corner near the road.

30
00:03:49,092 --> 00:03:54,852
(Q19) The pavilion is very well used at present by both football players and cricketers.

31
00:03:54,852 --> 00:04:03,324
It will stay where it is now – to the left of the line of trees and near to the river – handy for both the football and cricket pitches.

32
00:04:03,324 --> 00:04:05,824
(Q20) And finally, we'll be getting a new notice board for local information, and that will be directly on people's right as they go from the road into the recreation ground.

